# Generic tooling and LuaUnit migration plan

## Objective

Replace SoulSearch's existing `tools/` scripts with the reusable toolchain
currently staged under `NewTools/`, migrate the complete pure-Lua test suite
from the custom `tests/support/testlib.lua` framework to LuaUnit, and preserve
SoulSearch's source, package, and live DFHack behavior through the cutover.

The new `Build.ps1` behavior is the target contract. A default build must:

- syntax-check production and test Lua with `luac`;
- load optional machine-local configuration from `.env.local`;
- resolve the mod ID from `src/info.txt`;
- run `<mod-id> reload` through `dfhack-run.exe`; and
- fail when either syntax validation or the live reload fails.

`Publish.ps1` may deliberately call the build with `-LiveReload:$false` while
constructing a package. That explicit publish-only override does not change the
default interactive build contract.

## Architectural decisions

- Keep reusable mechanics in `tools/`; move SoulSearch-specific assertions into
  SoulSearch tests instead of embedding them in generic packaging scripts.
- Keep LuaUnit pinned to `3.5-1` in the repository-local `.luarocks/` tree.
- Discover test files by the existing `test_*.lua` / `*_test.lua` convention;
  support modules, fixtures, and `tests/run.lua` must not be treated as suites.
- Make `tests/run.lua` derive the repository root from its own location instead
  of interpreting the first LuaUnit argument as a path.
- Replace the copied `DOTHIS_TEST_FILES` name with a project-neutral runner
  contract. No copied script may retain DoThis or another sibling project's
  name, paths, commands, or package assumptions.
- Preserve test behavior and coverage during framework conversion. Passing
  fewer assertions or silently omitting a suite is not a successful migration.
- Keep source/package truth anchored to `src/`, including root `info.txt` and
  `scripts_modinstalled/`.
- Perform the final `NewTools/` to `tools/` replacement atomically after the new
  entrypoints and migrated test runner are proven together.

## Non-goals

- Do not change SoulSearch production behavior merely to simplify tests.
- Do not weaken DFHack stubs, module isolation, UI characterization, package
  payload checks, or live smoke requirements.
- Do not make LuaUnit or `.luarocks/` part of the published mod payload.
- Do not remove live reload from the default build.
- Do not treat a successful syntax check as proof that the LuaUnit suite,
  package, or live UI is correct.

## Phase 0 - Record the existing contracts and migration baseline

☑ Inventory the old and new parameters, environment variables, external
  dependencies, generated files, exit behavior, and callers for:
  - `Build.ps1` and `Check-LuaSyntax.ps1`;
  - `Test.ps1` and `Run-UnitTests.ps1`;
  - `Publish.ps1` and `VerifyPackage.ps1`;
  - `Common.ps1`.
☑ Record that default live reload is an accepted requirement of the new
  build, including the expected `DFHACK_RUNNER`,
  `DFHACK_DWARF_FORTRESS_ROOT`, `DFHACK_LUAC`, and
  `DFHACK_LUA_VERSION` configuration seams.
☑ Run the current custom test suite and record its exact suite, case,
  assertion, and failure totals where the current runner exposes them.
☑ Run the current syntax-only build and record the exact production-file
  count and compiler version.
☑ Capture the current source manifest and the manifests of the expanded and
  zip packages, including whether the zip has a package-root directory.
☑ Record the existing project-specific package invariants currently checked
  outside generic manifest equality, including:
  - `info.txt` at the package root;
  - `scripts_modinstalled/soulsearch.lua`;
  - the `--@module=true` and `--@enable=true` annotations;
  - `internal/soulsearch/keybindings.lua`.
☑ Add the baseline results to the execution-evidence table before changing
  the active `tools/` entrypoints.

Exit gate: the pre-migration test coverage, syntax scope, package shape,
SoulSearch-specific package invariants, and live-build target are explicit and
recorded.

### Phase 0 recorded baseline (2026-07-17)

The baseline was captured without restoring the deleted tracked
`tools/Publish.ps1` and `tools/VerifyPackage.ps1`, moving `NewTools/`, or
rebuilding `dist/`. The tracked `HEAD` versions define the old publish and
verification interfaces; the existing package artifacts record their last
output. This preserves the user's in-progress cutover changes.

#### Tool contract inventory

| Surface | Parameters and environment | Dependencies | Generated/process state | Exit behavior and callers |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Old `tools/Build.ps1` | `SourceDir=src/scripts_modinstalled`, `LuaPath=''`, `LuaMode=Auto|Luac|Lua`; no environment contract | `luac` candidates, with `lua`/`loadfile()` fallback | none | Collects all syntax failures, then throws; called by README/docs and the VS Code Build task, but not by the old publisher |
| New `Build.ps1` | `LuaCompiler`, `RequiredLuaVersion`, `LiveReload=$true`, `SourceDir=src`, `DFHackRunner`, `DwarfFortressRoot`, `ReloadOutputPath`, `EnvFile=.env.local`; reads `DFHACK_LUAC`, `DFHACK_LUA_VERSION`, `DFHACK_RUNNER`, and `DFHACK_DWARF_FORTRESS_ROOT` directly or through `.env.local` | `Check-LuaSyntax.ps1`, `Common.ps1`, `luac.exe`, and `dfhack-run.exe` | optional reload-output file; imports missing process variables from `.env.local`; performs `<mod-id> reload` | Throws on missing tools/metadata, syntax failure, or reload failure; targeted by the VS Code Build task and called with `-LiveReload:$false` by the new publisher |
| New `Check-LuaSyntax.ps1` | `LuaCompiler=$env:DFHACK_LUAC`, `RequiredLuaVersion=$env:DFHACK_LUA_VERSION`, `IncludeTests` | `luac.exe` or configured compiler | none | Throws on missing/wrong-version compiler and first syntax failure; called by new `Build.ps1` |
| New `Common.ps1` | no script parameters; exports `Import-EnvironmentFile`, `Get-ModInfo`, and `Resolve-DFHackRunner` | PowerShell/.NET only | may set previously absent process environment variables | Helper functions throw on invalid env entries, metadata, or runner resolution; dot-sourced by new Build and Publish |
| Old `tools/Test.ps1` | `LuaPath=''`; no environment contract | explicit/discovered `lua` interpreter | none | Throws on missing runner/interpreter or nonzero test exit; called by README, `tests/README.md`, and active feature plans |
| New `Run-UnitTests.ps1` | remaining arguments become `LuaUnitArgs`; temporarily reads/writes `LUA_PATH` and copied `DOTHIS_TEST_FILES` | exact LuaUnit `3.5-1`, `lua`, `luarocks`, and package-install access when the rock is absent | installs `.luarocks/`; temporarily replaces process test/Lua paths and restores them in `finally` | Throws during bootstrap/path setup, then uses `exit $LASTEXITCODE` for the Lua runner; targeted by the modified VS Code Unit Tests task |
| Old tracked `tools/Publish.ps1` | `SourceDir=src`, `OutputDir=dist`, `PackageName=''`, `NoRootFolder`, `NoExpandedFolder`; no environment contract | PowerShell copy/archive commands and old verifier | temporary staging tree, versioned zip, and optional expanded package | Throws on PowerShell/verifier failure and removes temp data in `finally`; called by README |
| New `Publish.ps1` | `SourceDir=src`, `OutputDir=dist`, `PackageName=''`; no direct environment parameters | new Common, Build, VerifyPackage, and PowerShell archive commands | temporary staging tree, versioned flat-root zip, and expanded package | Runs Build with live reload disabled, throws on build/package/verification failure, and removes temp data in `finally`; called by README after cutover |
| Old tracked `tools/VerifyPackage.ps1` | `SourceDir=src`, mandatory `ZipPath`/`PackageRoot`, optional `ExpandedPath`, `NoRootFolder` | .NET zip APIs and PowerShell filesystem reads | opens the zip; no durable output | Throws on payload-set or SoulSearch-bootstrap mismatch; called by old Publish |
| New `VerifyPackage.ps1` | mandatory `SourceDir`, `ZipPath`, and `ExpandedPath`; `PackageRoot=''` | PowerShell SHA-256 hashing and archive commands | temporary extraction tree removed in `finally` | Throws on source-shape, manifest, or content-hash mismatch; called by new Publish and intended as a standalone entrypoint |

Repository caller audit at this baseline:

- `.vscode/tasks.json` points Build at `Tools/Build.ps1` and Unit Tests at
  `Tools/Run-UnitTests.ps1`.
- `README.md` still documents `tools/Build.ps1`, the old `LuaPath`/`LuaMode`
  parameters, `tools/Test.ps1`, and `tools/Publish.ps1`.
- `tests/README.md` still documents `tools/Test.ps1` and the publisher boundary.
- `docs/revealed-unit-filtering.todo` still uses `tools/Test.ps1` and
  `tools/Build.ps1` as future gates.
- Inside `NewTools/`, Build calls Check/Common and Publish calls
  Build/Common/VerifyPackage.

The accepted target is the new default Build contract: syntax-check production
and test Lua, load optional `.env.local`, read the mod ID from `src/info.txt`,
and run `<mod-id> reload`. `DFHACK_RUNNER` or
`DFHACK_DWARF_FORTRESS_ROOT` locates the runner; `DFHACK_LUAC` selects the
compiler; `DFHACK_LUA_VERSION` optionally enforces its version.

#### Executed test and syntax baseline

- `./tools/Test.ps1` used
  `C:\Users\Sisco\AppData\Local\Programs\Lua\bin\lua.exe` and passed all 55
  explicitly registered suite modules: `325 test(s), 0 failure(s)`.
- The custom runner exposes case and failure totals but not a distinct assertion
  total, so the assertion baseline is recorded as unavailable rather than
  inferred.
- `./tools/Build.ps1` syntax-checked all 66 Lua files under
  `src/scripts_modinstalled/` and passed.
- The resolved compiler was
  `C:\Users\Sisco\AppData\Local\Programs\Lua\bin\luac.exe`, reporting
  `Lua 5.4.6`.

#### Source and package manifest baseline

Manifest fingerprints are SHA-256 hashes of the UTF-8 sequence of sorted
`normalized/path|file-SHA-256` rows. Zip paths are also recorded raw so the
archive-root contract remains visible. The complete per-path, per-artifact
hash manifest is recorded in `docs/tooling-migration-phase-0-manifest.md`.

| Artifact | Files | Manifest fingerprint | Shape |
| --- | ---: | --- | --- |
| Current `src/` | 67 | `60EAD277DB57EB03C2F197D0CEC4718008175FD6D6E036CE90F5BC5262E73D3D` | root `info.txt` plus `scripts_modinstalled/` |
| Existing `dist/SoulSearch/` | 65 | `39BB4A9C0B6A527446C6B2C1076373BB86ADC0544A7C2A9F870992FFDC55B680` | expanded package root is `SoulSearch/` |
| Existing `dist/SoulSearch-0.1.0.zip` | 65 | `39BB4A9C0B6A527446C6B2C1076373BB86ADC0544A7C2A9F870992FFDC55B680` after stripping the archive prefix | every file is beneath the single raw archive root `SoulSearch/` |

