## Completion criteria

This migration is complete only when:

- `tools/` contains the sole supported generic toolchain and `NewTools/` is no
  longer needed;
- default `tools/Build.ps1` performs syntax validation plus successful live
  `<mod-id> reload` using metadata from `src/info.txt`;
- every SoulSearch pure-Lua test is discovered and executed natively by pinned
  LuaUnit with no custom test framework remaining;
- the final test coverage is reconciled with the pre-migration baseline;
- publishing remains non-live and produces independently verified zip and
  expanded packages that exactly match the intended `src/` payload;
- SoulSearch-specific bootstrap/package invariants remain enforced by focused
  project tests;
- documentation, VS Code tasks, active plans, and command examples use only the
  new entrypoints and parameters;
- `.luarocks/`, `.env.local`, tests, tools, docs, and planning artifacts cannot
  enter the package; and
- the execution-evidence table records green automated, package, default live
  build, and focused in-game gates.
